{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778518053,"nonce":"RMHPUSdG2aSt4RAdImdXVPk07cY=","title":"Document research-app integration pattern (editable install + figure routing)","message":"Feedbax expects application packages (e.g., rlrmp) to be **editable** installs in a development checkout, not pip-installed library packages. The figure-routing system uses the application package’s `__file__` to find its repo root — which only works for editable installs. Once feedbax grows external users, this assumption needs explicit documentation.\n\nTopics to cover:\n- Why the dependency arrow goes only `application → feedbax` (feedbax is library, applications consume it).\n- Editable install requirement and recommended setup (`uv add -e ...`).\n- The entry-point registration pattern (`register_experiment_package`).\n- The `figure_routing` config schema and template variables.\n- The editable-install guard and what to do if it warns.\n- Anti-pattern: don’t `pip install` an application package; it’s research scaffolding, not a published library.\n\nA preliminary version was added to the feedbax README in a section titled \"Building application packages on feedbax\" (commit pending). This issue tracks the proper docs rebuild — likely a new `docs/integration.md` or equivalent once feedbax has a docs site.\n\nSurfaced from rlrmp `0f1af24` integration design discussion.","files":null}]}